  "id": "synthetic-validity",
  "term": "synthetic validity",
  "definition": "Synthetic validity refers to checking whether a computational modeling approach can correctly recover the model that generated simulated data. It is assessed with simulations that vary factors such as measurement error, amount of data, and similarity among models to see when model identification is valid or misleading.",
